[h1]Mixed Atmospheres: real gas and liquid mixtures[/h1]

[i]Draft Workshop description. Not published: posting it, and the release itself, wait for the author's authorization.[/i]

Mixed Atmospheres replaces Oxygen Not Included's gas and liquid simulation with its own solver. ONI still runs solids, buildings, duplicants, critters and plants; every gas and liquid in a new colony belongs to the mod.

[h2]What changes[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Gases mix and stay mixed.[/b] A tile holds oxygen, carbon dioxide, hydrogen and every other gas together instead of one element per tile. Carbon dioxide spreads through a room instead of pooling in a single pit, so scrubbers serve whole rooms.
[*][b]Liquids behave like liquids.[/b] Miscible liquids blend; immiscible liquids settle into layers you can see and manage. Liquid is nearly incompressible: there are no thousand-kilogram compressed liquid tiles.
[*][b]Pressure is physical.[/b] Gas compresses, and expands into vacuum. Boiling depends on pressure, and phase changes take or release latent heat.
[*][b]Pumps, pipes and filters carry mixtures.[/b] A pump takes the mixture at its intake, pipes carry it as it is, and a filter removes the constituent you pick and passes the rest.
[*][b]Breathing follows the mixture.[/b] By default a duplicant can breathe where oxygen is at least 15% by moles and 15 kPa partial pressure, CO₂ breathing limits default to Off. Enable them in Gameplay settings to enforce the optional 0.5% and 500 Pa thresholds. Oxygen is always required.
[*][b]You can see it.[/b] Composition and Breathability overlays, mixture hover readings and partial-pressure gauges show what your duplicants are actually breathing.
[/list]

[h2]Playing[/h2]
Enable the mod, restart when ONI asks, and start a [b]new[/b] colony. New colonies keep ONI's generated oxygen; nitrogen content has been removed. A ten-cycle oxygen shortfall is supplied as oxylite beside the printing pod. Build sustainable oxygen production, and arrange CO₂ removal if you enable its breathing limits. Older R&D saves are unsupported; start a new colony.

Settings are in the Mods screen (Settings button) or the in-game status panel: Gameplay opens first with the live CO₂ switch. Display & keys holds appearance and shortcuts. Advanced holds Default/Robust/Fast/Precise solver presets, technical controls, breathing thresholds, performance and saved presets. Solver settings and numeric thresholds are recorded per colony.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Platforms:[/b] 64-bit Windows and 64-bit Linux. macOS is not supported; the mod stays inactive there and the game runs as normal.
[*][b]Content:[/b] the base game and Spaced Out!, including multiple asteroids, rocket interiors and fluid cargo. The Frosty, Bionic, Prehistoric and Aquatic packs are not supported yet: while any of them is active, colonies keep ONI's own simulation and the main menu says so.
[*][b]Saves:[/b] existing colonies are not converted; they keep ONI's own simulation. [b]A colony started with Mixed Atmospheres needs the mod to load and cannot return to ONI's own simulation.[/b] Keep a copy of any colony you value.
[*][b]Game updates:[/b] each time ONI starts, the mod verifies every part of the game it depends on. After a Klei update that changes any of them, it stays inactive with a message and leaves your colonies untouched until a matching Mixed Atmospheres update is out. Updates that do not touch those parts need no mod update.
[*][b]Other mods:[/b] mods that change gases, liquids, pipes or the fluid simulation are unlikely to work with it.
[/list]

[h2]Performance[/h2]
The mixture solver does far more work than ONI's own fluid simulation. On large or busy asteroids the game clock runs slower than vanilla, the way a lower speed setting does; the camera, menus and pause stay responsive. It uses several CPU cores. Performance work continues.

[h2]If something goes wrong[/h2]
If the solver meets a state it cannot continue safely, gases and liquids stop visibly, the game tells you, and saving is refused so a bad state is never written; reload your last save. Please report problems with your [b]Player.log[/b]:
[list]
[*]Windows: %USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\Klei\Oxygen Not Included\Player.log
[*]Linux: ~/.config/unity3d/Klei/Oxygen Not Included/Player.log
[/list]
